  "title": "Leonell A NDE 6462",
  "date": "1967",
  "content": "I came out of the barber's shop, after having a haircut, and I was on the way home. My school is on the way, so I dropped in as usual and went to the playing field. There was a group of boys there, playing and climbing on the apparatus, which was there. I climbed onto a trapeze, and started to do abdominal exercises. The trapeze began to rock, and I slipped and fell on my back, hurting myself from my waist up to my head. When I came to, the Padre was there at my side, wiping with his hand something he had placed in my left hand and on my forehead. He exclaimed, 'He's not dead! He's not dead!' While I was lying on the ground, I remember speeding through a layer of clouds. I was dressed in the same clothes I had on, a pair of blue jeans, white T-shirt, sneakers. I was running towards a white light, which was very far off, and underneath it I recall a violet light. Suddenly I heard a voice. Turning round, I fell into an abyss, as if I had returned below. First, I heard a long sharp whistling noise in my ears, and then I saw shadows. As I came to my senses, I heard voices and the shadows became clearer. It was the boys looking at me lying face-up on the ground. The Padre asked me if I was okay. I replied, 'yes,' and then I got up and went home. When I took off my T-shirt at home my back was marked by the stones on the ground.",
